node_modules/

#: THE IDENTITY DATABASE AND EVERYTHING DERIVED FROM IT. This file holds
#: password hashes, encrypted face templates and mobile numbers -- the most
#: sensitive data in the program, and the one store with no second copy.
#:
#: `*.db` ALONE WAS NOT ENOUGH, and the gap was live: a backup taken before an
#: ALTER TABLE on 2026-09-12 was named `face-verify.db.bak-<date>`, which does
#: not END in `.db`, so it sat untracked and one `git add -A` from the remote.
#: SQLite's own sidecars (`-wal`, `-shm`, `-journal`) have the same shape and
#: the same contents.
#:
#: INTERIM. fverify is going to Postgres, at which point the database stops
#: being a file in the tree and these rules stop being the thing standing
#: between a stray backup and a push.
*.db
*.db-*
*.db.*
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
__pycache__/
.venv/
.env
/build/
/dist/
tools/

# Android build outputs
app/android/.gradle/
app/android/app/build/
app/android/build/
app/android/local.properties
